  "servings": 4,
  "summary": "Reinvent your morning routine with this hearty <b>Peruvian breakfast dish</b> featuring tender slow-braised beef inspired by classic Seco de Res. Marinated beef chuck is gently simmered in a vibrant green sauce made from blended fresh cilantro, yellow aji pepper paste, garlic, and fragrant spices. Once the meat is pull-apart tender, it is served over a bed of crispy skillet-cooked <b>sweet potato cubes</b>, creating a wonderful contrast between rich, savory stew and natural root vegetable sweetness. A fried egg cooked sunny-side-up tops the dish, adding a luscious runny yolk that enriches every bite. Pickled red onion salsa criolla adds a bright, acid-driven crunch that cuts through the hearty braised flavors. This fusion breakfast brings comforting Latin American dinner flavors to the morning table, making it an ideal choice for weekend brunches or special morning feasts that keep you satisfied for hours.",
